WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
On the Home screen, click Open project… and choose the project of the second tutorial.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.000
The project opens on the Graph page. Above the graph, Blocks, Folded and Table are three views of the same project.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Click the arrow at the top right to fold the settings panel for now.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Blocks shows the whole chain, left to right, in three bands: Preprocessing, Linear processing and Composition. Post comes last.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Each block is a card: its name, a summary line of its settings, and a bar on its left edge, green when the block is up to date. Click a card to select it.

6
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:35.000
The palette on the left lists the blocks that can be added, in groups: Sources, Frames, Image, Post and Composition. A block is dragged onto the chain or double-clicked, and a block that cannot be added here is greyed.

7
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Click the zoom box: it offers fixed sizes, and Show all.

8
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Ctrl and the mouse wheel zoom the graph.

9
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Click Show all: the whole graph fits in the window.

10
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Click Folded.

11
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Folded draws each stack as one card: its name, its number of sessions and lights, its stacking method and a row of dots. Astrometry, Gradient, Denoise, Color and Post stay as they were.

12
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Click Table.

13
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Table: one row per session, under the name of its stack. The files are in the Lights, Darks, Flats and Bias columns, then come the settings of the stack. The Common row on top serves every session.

14
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Click Add session: a second row arrives.

15
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:18.000
The new session is empty: no lights, darks, flats or bias. With two sessions, the Common row offers cells for darks, flats and bias shared by both.

16
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Click Undo in the notice: the session is removed and the project is as it was.

17
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Add stack starts another stack at the bottom of the table, with one session: that is how a project holds several workflows. + columns, the Files list and Only differences sit beside it.

18
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Click a session’s cell, then the settings button on the right edge.

19
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:39.000
The settings panel on the right lists what the session holds, with the Open frames button to add or change its frames.

20
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Click Blocks again.

21
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.000
It is the same project and the same chain: the views only change how it is shown.

22
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.000
Click a block, then the settings button on the right edge.

23
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:58.000
The panel shows the settings of the selected block: here the rule and the thresholds of Selection.

24
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:03.000
The GPU list above the graph chooses what computes: Automatic, or the processor alone.

25
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:09.000
Run starts the computation. It is greyed here: everything is already up to date.
